part bank_half
  tally 2
  note "T, M2 (issues #167, #114), DONE gate 2: the bank half of the prototype's reality R7 (engine/spec/verification/goldens.md: G2, G4, G5), restated over the prototype's bank history (ledger.json, synthetic, seed 20261017; records/, written by to_tally.py). Its plan is the part of blocks 01-month and 04-employment the ledger's links reach: my pay (my_job, 12 000 gross), my wife's (wife_job, 7 000 gross), each paid in the month after the month it earns, and the rent of 3 200 on the 1st. Everything else in the ledger is an observed movement the plan doesn't hold, with its category. The model's header is reality.tally (the bank run, to 2027-01-31) or one of r7/'s (the forward half, to a horizon), which each declare the month and year indexes."
  note "The pay law is the prototype's employment_pl@2022 as household X writes it (integration/amendments/real11/c1/law/pl/employment.tally) and m1/goldens/y22/model.tally restates it: ZUS on the gross up to the year's 30-fold cap, health on the rest, the advance on the running base to whole zloty less a twelfth of the reducing amount. The gross is job_pl@1's in.gross * p.index.wage, and the rent najem@1's in.rent * p.index.prices: both indexes are 1 until 2027-01-01, so the bank run reads the stated figures. Not stated: child relief and residence, which no asked figure reads. The prototype ran its 2026 law over its whole past (make-ledger.ts: one run of the model), so the rows here govern from 2024."
  note "Pay days: over the bank history (the modelled past) my pay is planned on the 5th, the middle of the 3rd–7th window, and my wife's on the 10th. From plan_from on, the planned pays fall where the prototype plans them: an inflow over a window on its last day (window@1), the 7th, and my wife's on the 10th, each moved to the business day before (bd prev) by the prototype's calendar."

source ledger "the prototype's bank history, engine/tests/m2/bank/ledger.json, made by make-ledger.ts (seed 20261017); synthetic"

source prototype "the prototype's blocks 01-month.json and 04-employment.json and its template employment_pl@2022 (engine/spec/verification/blocks)"

source calendar_pl "the prototype's calendar.ts: Polish public holidays by the ustawa o dniach wolnych od pracy (New Year, Epiphany, Easter and Easter Monday, 1 and 3 May, Pentecost, Corpus Christi, 15 August, 1 and 11 November, 25 and 26 December, Wigilia from 2025)"

unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

kind bank_line: transfers
  attr cat: key category
  note "a row of the prototype's ledger, with its category"

kind job

kind person

index category = [codzienne, czynsz, faktury, inne, inwestycje, pit_firma, pit_roczny, skladki_zus, vat, wynagrodzenie]

index zus_part = [pension, disability, sickness]

place dostawcy: outside lives 2024-01-01..

place ike: accounts PLN lives 2024-01-01..

place klienci: outside lives 2024-01-01..

place konto: accounts PLN lives 2024-01-01..

place maklerskie: accounts PLN lives 2024-01-01..

place pracodawca: outside lives 2024-01-01..

place pracodawca_zony: outside lives 2024-01-01..

place sklepy: outside lives 2024-01-01..

place urzad_skarbowy: outside lives 2024-01-01..

place wynajmujacy: outside lives 2024-01-01..

place zus: outside lives 2024-01-01..

input bank: observed
  note "the ledger's rows, one part a month (records/)"

input ee_rate[z in zus_part]: num

input health_rate: num

input holidays_pl: calendar

input inflation: num

input kup_month: money PLN

input learn_first: date

input learn_last: date

input pay_dom[j in job]: int

input pit_reduction_month: money PLN

input plan_dom[j in job]: int

input plan_from: month

input prices: num

input proj_wage: money PLN

input rent: money PLN

input salary[j in job]: money PLN

input wage_growth: num

input zus_cap_factor: int

band pit_scale(x: num PLN): num PLN
  note "art. 27 ust. 1: the tax before reliefs, after the reducing amount"

def gross[j in job, m in month]: num PLN = salary[j] * wage_index[year_of(m)] at start_of(m)
  note "job_pl@1: in.gross * p.index.wage, not rounded"

def price_index[y in cal_year]: num at start_of(y)
  note "01-month.json index.prices: 1 from 2000-01-01, then before * (1 + assume.inflation) each year from 2027-01-01"
  rule initial = 1 when pos(y) == 1
  rule next = price_index[y - 1] * (1 + inflation) when pos(y) > 1

def wage_index[y in cal_year]: num at start_of(y)
  note "01-month.json index.wage: 1 from 2000-01-01, then before * (1 + assume.wage_growth) each year from 2027-01-01"
  rule initial = 1 when pos(y) == 1
  rule next = wage_index[y - 1] * (1 + wage_growth) when pos(y) > 1

def zus_base[j in job, m in month]: num PLN = max(0, min(gross[j, m], zus_cap_factor * proj_wage - sum(gross[j, k] for k in month where year_of(k) == year_of(m) and k < m))) at start_of(m)
  note "employment_pl@2022 soc.cap_base: the gross up to the year's cap (30 times the projected average wage) less the gross before the month"

def emp_zus[j in job, m in month]: money PLN = round(zus_base[j, m] * ee_rate[pension], minor(PLN), half-up) + round(zus_base[j, m] * ee_rate[disability], minor(PLN), half-up) + round(gross[j, m] * ee_rate[sickness], minor(PLN), half-up) at start_of(m)

def emp_health[j in job, m in month]: money PLN = round((gross[j, m] - emp_zus[j, m]) * health_rate, minor(PLN), half-up) at start_of(m)

def emp_pit_base[j in job, m in month]: money PLN = round(max(0, gross[j, m] - emp_zus[j, m] - kup_month), 1, half-up) at start_of(m)

def emp_cum[j in job, m in month]: money PLN = sum(emp_pit_base[j, k] for k in month where year_of(k) == year_of(m) and k <= m) at start_of(m)

def emp_pit_adv[j in job, m in month]: money PLN = max(0, round(pit_scale(emp_cum[j, m]) - pit_scale(emp_cum[j, m] - emp_pit_base[j, m]) - pit_reduction_month, 1, half-up)) at start_of(m)
  note "art. 32: the advance on the running base, less a twelfth of the reducing amount, to whole zloty"

def emp_net[j in job, m in month]: money PLN = round(gross[j, m] - emp_zus[j, m] - emp_health[j, m] - emp_pit_adv[j, m], minor(PLN), half-up) at start_of(m)

def pay_day[j in job, m in month]: date at start_of(m)
  rule history = add_months(day_of(m, pay_dom[j]), 1)
  rule planned beats history = schedule(month_of(add_months(start_of(m), 1)), plan_dom[j], preceding, holidays_pl) when m >= plan_from

def spend_daily: money PLN at learn_last
  note "01-month.json: spending is hist_daily(codzienne, 365) * index.prices, the average daily spending of the last 365 days of the bank history, following prices (G5)"
  rule learned = round(sum(o.cash.amount for o in bank_line over learn_first .. learn_last where o.cat == codzienne) / (days_between(learn_first, learn_last) + 1) * prices, minor(PLN), half-up) when covered(konto, learn_first .. learn_last)

move my_pay[m in month]: transfers
  on pay_day[my_job, m]
  at start_of(m)
  for m
  leg cash from pracodawca to konto amount emp_net[my_job, m]

move rent_pay[m in month]: transfers
  on day_of(m, 1)
  at start_of(m)
  for m
  leg cash from konto to wynajmujacy amount round(rent * price_index[year_of(m)], minor(PLN), half-up)

move wife_pay[m in month]: transfers
  on pay_day[wife_job, m]
  at start_of(m)
  for m
  leg cash from pracodawca_zony to konto amount emp_net[wife_job, m]

version household
  cite prototype
  governs always
  known 2023-12-31
  person + [me] lives 1991-02-14..
  person + [wife] lives 1992-07-03..
  job + [my_job] lives 2024-01-01..
  job + [wife_job] lives 2024-01-01..
  salary[my_job] = 12000 "01-month.json: my_job, person me, gross 12 000"
  salary[wife_job] = 7000 "04-employment.json: wife_job, person wife, gross 7 000"
  pay_dom[my_job] = 5 "01-month.json: my pay between the 3rd and the 7th of the next month; over the history, the 5th, the window's middle"
  pay_dom[wife_job] = 10 "04-employment.json: the wife's pay about the 10th of the next month"
  plan_dom[my_job] = 7 "01-month.json: my_tax pay_on next_month:3-7, an inflow planned on the window's last day (window@1), bd prev"
  plan_dom[wife_job] = 10 "04-employment.json: wife_tax pay_on next_month:10, bd prev"
  plan_from = 2026-10 "the first month whose pay the prototype plans: October's, paid in November, after today (2026-10-17)"
  rent = 3200 "01-month.json: rent 3 200 on the 1st"
  learn_first = 2025-10-17 "01-month.json: hist_daily(codzienne, 365), the 365 days before today (2026-10-17)"
  learn_last = 2026-10-16 "the last of those days, the day before today"
  prices = 1 "01-month.json: index.prices is 1 until 2027-01-01, flat over the learning window (G5)"
  inflation = 0 governs 2024-01-01..2026-12-31 "01-month.json: index.prices is 1 until 2027-01-01"
  wage_growth = 0 governs 2024-01-01..2026-12-31 "01-month.json: index.wage is 1 until 2027-01-01"

version openings
  cite ledger
  governs always
  known 2024-01-01
  opening[ike] = 30000 at 2024-01-01 start "ledger.json row 1, otwarcie"
  opening[konto] = 12000 at 2024-01-01 start "ledger.json row 0, otwarcie"
  opening[maklerskie] = 20000 at 2024-01-01 start "ledger.json row 2, otwarcie"

version employment_pl
  cite prototype
  governs always
  known 2023-12-31
  ee_rate[disability] = 0.015 "employment_pl@2022: the employee's disability share"
  ee_rate[pension] = 0.0976 "employment_pl@2022: the employee's pension share"
  ee_rate[sickness] = 0.0245 "employment_pl@2022: sickness"
  health_rate = 0.09 "employment_pl@2022: health, 9 %"
  kup_month = 250 "employment_pl@2022: costs of earning, 250 a month"
  pit_reduction_month = 300 "employment_pl@2022: a twelfth of 3 600"
  zus_cap_factor = 30 "04-employment.json zus.annual_cap: 30 * p.wage.projected_average (ustawa o sus art. 19 ust. 1)"
  pit_scale: [0, 120000] = x * 0.12 - 3600 "employment_pl@2022: art. 27 ust. 1, first threshold"
  pit_scale: (120000, inf) = 10800 + (x - 120000) * 0.32 "employment_pl@2022: art. 27 ust. 1, second threshold"

version projected_wage
  cite prototype
  governs always
  known 2023-12-31
  proj_wage = 7824 governs 2024-01-01..2024-12-31 "04-employment.json wage.projected_average: obwieszczenie MRiPS na 2024 r."
  proj_wage = 8673 governs 2025-01-01..2025-12-31 "ustawa budżetowa 2025"
  proj_wage = 9420 governs 2026-01-01.. "M.P. 2025 poz. 1206; the prototype holds it past its last entry (law held after today)"

version holidays
  cite calendar_pl
  governs always
  known 2023-12-31
  holidays_pl = calendar(weekends [sat, sun], added [2024-01-01, 2024-01-06, 2024-03-31, 2024-04-01, 2024-05-01, 2024-05-03, 2024-05-19, 2024-05-30, 2024-08-15, 2024-11-01, 2024-11-11, 2024-12-25, 2024-12-26, 2025-01-01, 2025-01-06, 2025-04-20, 2025-04-21, 2025-05-01, 2025-05-03, 2025-06-08, 2025-06-19, 2025-08-15, 2025-11-01, 2025-11-11, 2025-12-24, 2025-12-25, 2025-12-26, 2026-01-01, 2026-01-06, 2026-04-05, 2026-04-06, 2026-05-01, 2026-05-03, 2026-05-24, 2026-06-04, 2026-08-15, 2026-11-01, 2026-11-11, 2026-12-24, 2026-12-25, 2026-12-26, 2027-01-01, 2027-01-06, 2027-03-28, 2027-03-29, 2027-05-01, 2027-05-03, 2027-05-16, 2027-05-27, 2027-08-15, 2027-11-01, 2027-11-11, 2027-12-24, 2027-12-25, 2027-12-26, 2028-01-01, 2028-01-06, 2028-04-16, 2028-04-17, 2028-05-01, 2028-05-03, 2028-06-04, 2028-06-15, 2028-08-15, 2028-11-01, 2028-11-11, 2028-12-24, 2028-12-25, 2028-12-26, 2029-01-01, 2029-01-06, 2029-04-01, 2029-04-02, 2029-05-01, 2029-05-03, 2029-05-20, 2029-05-31, 2029-08-15, 2029-11-01, 2029-11-11, 2029-12-24, 2029-12-25, 2029-12-26, 2030-01-01, 2030-01-06, 2030-04-21, 2030-04-22, 2030-05-01, 2030-05-03, 2030-06-09, 2030-06-20, 2030-08-15, 2030-11-01, 2030-11-11, 2030-12-24, 2030-12-25, 2030-12-26, 2031-01-01, 2031-01-06, 2031-04-13, 2031-04-14, 2031-05-01, 2031-05-03, 2031-06-01, 2031-06-12, 2031-08-15, 2031-11-01, 2031-11-11, 2031-12-24, 2031-12-25, 2031-12-26, 2032-01-01, 2032-01-06, 2032-03-28, 2032-03-29, 2032-05-01, 2032-05-03, 2032-05-16, 2032-05-27, 2032-08-15, 2032-11-01, 2032-11-11, 2032-12-24, 2032-12-25, 2032-12-26, 2033-01-01, 2033-01-06, 2033-04-17, 2033-04-18, 2033-05-01, 2033-05-03, 2033-06-05, 2033-06-16, 2033-08-15, 2033-11-01, 2033-11-11, 2033-12-24, 2033-12-25, 2033-12-26, 2034-01-01, 2034-01-06, 2034-04-09, 2034-04-10, 2034-05-01, 2034-05-03, 2034-05-28, 2034-06-08, 2034-08-15, 2034-11-01, 2034-11-11, 2034-12-24, 2034-12-25, 2034-12-26, 2035-01-01, 2035-01-06, 2035-03-25, 2035-03-26, 2035-05-01, 2035-05-03, 2035-05-13, 2035-05-24, 2035-08-15, 203